The class GeminiChatCompletionClient is internal sealed and inherits from an internal base class ClientBase, so I cannot instantiate or subclass it in tests. The LogUsage method is private, so I cannot call it directly. However, the ProcessChatResponse method is private and calls LogUsage internally.

I will write tests for the public method GenerateChatMessageAsync or any other public method that calls ProcessChatResponse internally, so that the LogUsage call is exercised indirectly and the ILogger.LogInformation call on line 824 is covered.

I will create a test that mocks ILogger and verifies that LogInformation is called when the token counts are valid, by invoking GenerateChatMessageAsync with a suitable GeminiResponse that leads to ProcessChatResponse being called.

I will submit the test now. It will use Moq for ILogger and create minimal stubs for GeminiResponse and related types as needed.

